Laya Blackwell includes inference computations and request semantics adapted
from Laya, developed by Convai Innovations and distributed under Apache-2.0.

Upstream model: https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya
Upstream SDK: https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya
SDK version used: 0.3.9

The model execution in src/laya_blackwell/model.py and response preparation
in src/laya_blackwell/protocol.py have been modified for this engine. Changes
include resident BF16 linear weights, precomputed rotary values, a fused
rotary kernel, selective final-head outputs, bounded request preparation,
and NumPy response formatting.

The ModernBERT execution follows the Transformers implementation, distributed
under Apache-2.0, with changes to layout, precision handling and execution.
https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/v5.17.0/src/transformers/models/modernbert/modeling_modernbert.py

A copy of the Apache-2.0 terms is in licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.
Model weights are downloaded separately and are not included in this package.

The optional FastEngine packages native CUDA normalization and attention
kernels under their retained BSD-3-Clause terms. Its normalization and fused
reduction follow PyTorch's Welford operation order; its attention kernels
instantiate pinned PyTorch, CUTLASS and FlashAttention templates. Licenses,
author lists and revision-specific attribution are included in
src/laya_blackwell/fast/native/NOTICE.txt and the adjacent license files.
The package metadata includes BSD-3-Clause alongside MIT and Apache-2.0.

FastEngine's request preparation and native response formatting also adapt
the Laya SDK protocol under Apache-2.0. Changes include batched Rust
tokenization, packed host transfers, and native NumPy FP32 formatting loops.
The model adapter adds exact BF16 projections, matched partial reductions,
specialized attention and frozen token-local tables, without caching answers.
